lede-orilla = An abandoned lighthouse, a radio that starts playing again and a town hiding what happened the night of the storm.
lede-neon = A night courier receives a package nobody wants to pick up, in a city that never turns off its lights.
lede-pan = A chemistry teacher becomes the most feared baker in the desert. His sourdough shows no mercy.
lede-raras = A town, Christmas lights that blink on their own and a basement nobody comes back from with Wi-Fi.
lede-carton = Eight robbers in cardboard masks plan the heist of the century at the packaging factory.
lede-tronos = Seven kingdoms fight over the only wooden chair that doesn't wobble. Winter brings splinters.
lede-oso = A fine-dining chef comes home to save the family bakery. Yes, chef.
lede-separ = Employees who forget their lives when they take the elevator. Worst of all, they can't remember where they parked either.
lede-oficina = A documentary about a paper distributor where nobody distributes anything.
lede-lazo = A rodeo coach ends up managing a football team. He doesn't know what offside is. Doesn't matter.
lede-espejo = Stories about the technology we use every day and the "Accept" button nobody reads.
lede-hipotecas = Four siblings fight to inherit the family empire: a flat with a 40-year mortgage.
lede-pixel = An eight-bit plumber discovers that his world ends at the right edge of the screen.
lede-lobos = A school trip, a forest with no signal and a moon that's far too big.
lede-cometas = Three sisters inherit a plant nursery that actually sells kites, and none of them can fly one.
lede-altamar = A year aboard a research sailboat following the humpback whales of the Atlantic.
lede-jujutsu = A student swallows a cursed finger and now has to pass exorcism and maths on the same day.
lede-komi = The most popular girl in school wants to make a hundred friends without saying a word. She carries a notebook and plenty of patience.
lede-naruton = A blond ninja yells all day long that he'll be the village chief. First he has to pay for the ramen he owes.
lede-titos = Three walls protect the city from giant uncles who only want to say hi and stay for lunch.
lede-sprite-fright = Some teenagers camp in a forest where not every mushroom is friendly. Featured test: poster, gallery and preview from YouTube.

